    "done_when": "Reported by s25-picker from a whole-suite run at a08a2baae (run r-20261002T202015024095-suite-at-head, solo-rerun.log). tests/test_fleet_counter_coverage.py::test_the_blocked_bucket_is_derived_from_the_attention_set fails alone. The test's _emitted_states reads the literal `state = \"...\"` assignments from inspect.getsource(recovery._watch_verdict). The stall verdict is now returned by the pure helper recovery._stall_reading (`return \"stalled\", ...`), which the snapshot reuse path also calls. So \"stalled\" drops out of the scraped set and the subset assertion fails. The behaviour is right; the test reads too narrow a source. The node makes _emitted_states read the reducer's emitting helpers as well: at least _stall_reading, matching the first element of its literal returns. It states in the docstring why the helper is part of the emitter. No product file changes. The file passes; the two snapshot test files, tests/test_an_unchanged_run_costs_one_stat.py and tests/test_a_reused_snapshot_takes_the_callers_stall_window.py, also pass. The declared negative control is executed and logged, and its log shows the failing assertion is the subset assertion.",
